1
00:00:30,800 --> 00:00:31,399
Oh my god!

2
00:00:31,559 --> 00:00:32,240
Star Reporter Shen!

3
00:00:32,960 --> 00:00:33,600
Hello, hello, hello!

4
00:00:34,320 --> 00:00:35,719
I'm Factory Director Ma Guowen.

5
00:00:36,119 --> 00:00:37,000
Hello, Director Ma.

6
00:00:37,359 --> 00:00:37,920
Sorry to keep you waiting.

7
00:00:37,920 --> 00:00:39,600
I'll show you around before the interview.

8
00:00:39,719 --> 00:00:40,359
Come on, let's go.

9
00:03:01,840 --> 00:03:02,680
Hurry and take photos.

10
00:03:07,080 --> 00:03:07,879
What's going on here?

11
00:03:08,439 --> 00:03:10,639
Isn't this the car in Cao Jun's photo?

12
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:11,680
Last time I came,

13
00:03:11,680 --> 00:03:12,680
you swore up and down

14
00:03:12,680 --> 00:03:13,639
that it wasn't at your factory.

15
00:03:15,039 --> 00:03:17,280
Yeah. I didn't dare say it last time.

16
00:03:19,560 --> 00:03:19,960
Fine.

17
00:03:20,800 --> 00:03:22,280
Good thing you called me on your own.

18
00:03:23,000 --> 00:03:24,039
When did this car get here?

19
00:03:26,599 --> 00:03:27,639
Back around 2000.

20
00:03:28,080 --> 00:03:29,360
Over ten years, and it wasn't scrapped?

21
00:03:29,360 --> 00:03:30,039
Why?

22
00:03:32,039 --> 00:03:32,599
Look,

23
00:03:32,879 --> 00:03:34,400
give me the salvage certificate

24
00:03:34,400 --> 00:03:36,000
that traffic control gave you back then.

25
00:03:36,759 --> 00:03:37,400
Let me take a look.

26
00:03:39,719 --> 00:03:40,800
It's been too long.

27
00:03:40,800 --> 00:03:42,080
I don't even know where it was put.

28
00:03:42,319 --> 00:03:42,960
Can't find it now.

29
00:03:43,960 --> 00:03:45,000
You never had one, did you?

30
00:03:46,439 --> 00:03:48,159
What's the real story here?

31
00:03:53,879 --> 00:03:54,560
Back then,

32
00:03:54,680 --> 00:03:55,439
at first glance,

33
00:03:55,680 --> 00:03:57,240
I could tell something was off with this car.

34
00:03:58,840 --> 00:04:01,319
I can tell it's off at first glance too.

35
00:04:01,800 --> 00:04:02,680
What kind of problem?

36
00:04:02,719 --> 00:04:04,560
Why didn't you call the police back then?

37
00:04:17,759 --> 00:04:18,399
Are you done taking photos?

38
00:04:18,519 --> 00:04:19,000
All done.

39
00:04:19,920 --> 00:04:20,920
I've noticed something about you.

40
00:04:21,879 --> 00:04:22,879
You either know nothing,

41
00:04:23,800 --> 00:04:24,959
or you're lying through your teeth.

42
00:04:25,759 --> 00:04:26,079
Tell you what.

43
00:04:26,319 --> 00:04:26,839
It's freezing out here.

44
00:04:26,879 --> 00:04:27,680
Come back to the station with me,

45
00:04:28,040 --> 00:04:29,079
and we'll talk somewhere warm.

46
00:04:29,199 --> 00:04:29,839
Let's go. Take him with us.

47
00:04:30,399 --> 00:04:30,720
Move it.

48
00:04:31,920 --> 00:04:32,439
Officer Gao...

49
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:35,199
I'll talk! I'll talk!

50
00:04:35,879 --> 00:04:36,439
It's just...

51
00:04:38,199 --> 00:04:39,120
I was scared.

52
00:04:39,959 --> 00:04:41,680
We can't afford to cross that man.

53
00:04:41,959 --> 00:04:42,600
Who is it?

54
00:04:43,120 --> 00:04:43,800
What are you scared of?

55
00:04:43,800 --> 00:04:44,839
Who could be above the law?

56
00:04:49,360 --> 00:04:50,839
Director of Industry and Commerce.

57
00:04:51,639 --> 00:04:52,399
Zheng Aimin.

58
00:04:54,279 --> 00:04:55,639
The former director.

59
00:05:04,000 --> 00:05:05,199
Who else knows about this?

60
00:05:05,920 --> 00:05:07,199
I only told my cousin.

61
00:05:08,639 --> 00:05:11,079
And then something happened to him...

62
00:05:11,879 --> 00:05:12,639
That terrified me.

63
00:05:13,240 --> 00:05:13,839
Scared of what?

64
00:05:15,680 --> 00:05:17,120
I was afraid I got him killed.

65
00:05:19,439 --> 00:05:19,959
What do you mean?

66
00:05:20,040 --> 00:05:20,959
Back then...

67
00:05:21,360 --> 00:05:23,680
I was scared that obeying his order

68
00:05:23,680 --> 00:05:24,959
to scrap the car

69
00:05:25,360 --> 00:05:26,720
would bring the police to my door later.

70
00:05:27,199 --> 00:05:29,759
So I asked my cousin over to discuss it

71
00:05:29,759 --> 00:05:30,519
and give me some advice.

72
00:05:31,519 --> 00:05:32,879
What did you drag me over here for?

73
00:05:32,920 --> 00:05:33,639
Take a look at this for me.

74
00:05:33,680 --> 00:05:35,199
Look at what? I'm supposed to be at work!

75
00:05:35,759 --> 00:05:37,040
Anyone can tell this car was in a wreck.

76
00:05:38,079 --> 00:05:39,720
They made me scrap it without any papers.

77
00:05:40,160 --> 00:05:40,720
Look at it.

78
00:05:40,759 --> 00:05:41,920
What? Without any papers at all,

79
00:05:41,920 --> 00:05:43,040
you dared take this job?

80
00:05:43,040 --> 00:05:43,920
What the hell is wrong with you?

81
00:05:44,360 --> 00:05:45,199
You're unbelievable.

82
00:05:46,879 --> 00:05:47,600
Just this car...

83
00:05:49,800 --> 00:05:50,519
Wait, this car...

84
00:05:52,040 --> 00:05:53,079
Who owns it?

85
00:05:54,079 --> 00:05:54,639
I don't know.

86
00:05:57,040 --> 00:05:58,519
Then who told you to take it in?

87
00:06:04,399 --> 00:06:04,920
Who was it?

88
00:06:06,600 --> 00:06:07,360
Fine, don't tell me then.

89
00:06:07,399 --> 00:06:08,399
I don't even want to get involved in your crap.

90
00:06:08,439 --> 00:06:09,240
I've got to get back to work.

91
00:06:09,399 --> 00:06:10,120
I'll tell you!

92
00:06:14,319 --> 00:06:15,519
Brother Li came to me.

93
00:06:15,759 --> 00:06:17,600
He drives for an official.

94
00:06:17,839 --> 00:06:18,319
An official?

95
00:06:19,680 --> 00:06:20,160
Who?

96
00:06:20,680 --> 00:06:22,800
Zheng Aimin, head of Industry & Commerce.

97
00:06:24,279 --> 00:06:24,879
Director Zheng?

98
00:06:27,519 --> 00:06:28,800
What's Director Zheng got to do with this?

99
00:06:28,959 --> 00:06:29,639
I don't know.

100
00:06:33,240 --> 00:06:34,560
This is clearly a hit-and-run wreck!

101
00:06:34,800 --> 00:06:35,720
Why would he get involved in this...

102
00:06:35,959 --> 00:06:37,000
What for?

103
00:06:41,199 --> 00:06:43,079
Why drag you into this out of nowhere?

104
00:07:10,879 --> 00:07:11,519
It's him.

105
00:07:13,600 --> 00:07:13,959
Who?

106
00:07:14,399 --> 00:07:15,279
You know the owner?

107
00:07:15,879 --> 00:07:16,959
No, I don't. No.

108
00:07:17,120 --> 00:07:18,000
How would I know him?

109
00:07:20,079 --> 00:07:20,639
Bro.

110
00:07:21,079 --> 00:07:21,839
Take a look at this newspaper.

111
00:07:23,000 --> 00:07:23,720
It's from today.

112
00:07:24,519 --> 00:07:25,240
Look at this car.

113
00:07:26,720 --> 00:07:29,639
"Taxi driver tragically killed."

114
00:07:30,319 --> 00:07:31,959
"Severe car crash."

115
00:07:34,439 --> 00:07:35,680
Look at this car, it...

116
00:07:35,680 --> 00:07:36,759
Aren't the two connected somehow?

117
00:07:41,199 --> 00:07:42,319
Hit-and-run.

118
00:07:43,800 --> 00:07:44,759
Hit-and-run.

119
00:07:45,399 --> 00:07:46,439
You knew about it?

120
00:07:47,560 --> 00:07:48,279
No, I don't.

121
00:07:48,759 --> 00:07:49,920
How would I know that?

122
00:07:50,279 --> 00:07:51,120
Anyway, uh...

123
00:07:51,439 --> 00:07:52,120
Get back to work.

124
00:07:52,120 --> 00:07:52,959
I'm heading to work.

125
00:07:53,519 --> 00:07:54,199
Wait, Bro.

126
00:07:54,639 --> 00:07:55,519
I asked you here

127
00:07:55,519 --> 00:07:56,360
to give me advice.

128
00:07:56,399 --> 00:07:57,160
Do whatever the hell you want.

129
00:07:57,160 --> 00:07:57,600
I've got work to do.

130
00:07:57,639 --> 00:07:58,839
Come on, you're my brother.

131
00:07:58,839 --> 00:07:59,519
Help me out.

132
00:07:59,519 --> 00:08:01,319
Let me finish my shift first.

133
00:08:01,319 --> 00:08:02,319
Just go on with your work.

134
00:08:02,800 --> 00:08:03,319
Wait, Bro...

135
00:08:03,319 --> 00:08:04,120
Look, go do your work.

136
00:08:04,160 --> 00:08:04,759
Go on.

137
00:08:05,040 --> 00:08:07,439
Later, I lied to Brother Li.

138
00:08:07,519 --> 00:08:09,040
I said I'd destroyed the car.

139
00:08:09,439 --> 00:08:10,000
And then?

140
00:08:10,279 --> 00:08:11,439
Then...

141
00:08:12,920 --> 00:08:14,000
later on, it seemed he

142
00:08:14,079 --> 00:08:15,560
found out who owned the car.

143
00:08:15,759 --> 00:08:16,120
Who?

144
00:08:16,519 --> 00:08:17,439
That, I don't know.

145
00:08:17,439 --> 00:08:18,160
My cousin didn't tell me.

146
00:08:18,959 --> 00:08:20,439
He said I shouldn't know too much.

147
00:08:20,439 --> 00:08:21,279
Knowing too much

148
00:08:21,519 --> 00:08:22,319
isn't good for anyone.

149
00:08:24,279 --> 00:08:25,319
I just feel this car

150
00:08:25,399 --> 00:08:27,759
is definitely tied to my cousin's death.

151
00:08:42,000 --> 00:08:43,519
Chen Yuan just went to the police station,

152
00:08:43,679 --> 00:08:44,799
but he couldn't see his dad either.

153
00:08:45,639 --> 00:08:46,519
Tell me, how could his dad

154
00:08:46,519 --> 00:08:48,240
get into such a huge mess?

155
00:08:50,200 --> 00:08:50,799
Do you think

156
00:08:51,679 --> 00:08:54,120
you could help pull some strings?

157
00:08:57,120 --> 00:08:58,840
Mind your own business.

158
00:09:08,200 --> 00:09:10,159
What's wrong with this gas stove?

159
00:09:10,159 --> 00:09:11,440
It won't even light.

160
00:09:12,159 --> 00:09:13,960
I'm fuming here, you want some of that?

161
00:09:15,240 --> 00:09:17,320
What are you yelling for?

162
00:09:17,440 --> 00:09:19,120
I'm fuming too!

163
00:09:29,000 --> 00:09:30,279
What did the police say?

164
00:09:30,399 --> 00:09:31,519
How should I know?

165
00:09:35,240 --> 00:09:36,039
Calm down.

166
00:09:36,639 --> 00:09:37,799
Tell Chen Yuan

167
00:09:37,840 --> 00:09:38,879
to stop running around blindly.

168
00:09:39,559 --> 00:09:40,559
I'll figure something out

169
00:09:40,559 --> 00:09:41,519
and pull some strings for him.

170
00:09:47,519 --> 00:09:48,360
I'll get it, I'll get it.

171
00:09:49,039 --> 00:09:49,799
Who is it?

172
00:09:50,159 --> 00:09:50,879
Coming!

173
00:09:56,519 --> 00:09:56,919
Hello.

174
00:09:57,240 --> 00:09:58,159
Is Zheng Aimin home?

175
00:09:59,320 --> 00:09:59,960
And you are...?

176
00:10:21,240 --> 00:10:22,279
Young officer,

177
00:10:23,279 --> 00:10:24,720
I've been waiting here for quite a while.

178
00:10:25,120 --> 00:10:26,679
Why don't we get started?

179
00:10:34,919 --> 00:10:35,519
Director Zheng.

180
00:10:35,759 --> 00:10:36,759
Sorry to take up your time.

181
00:10:37,120 --> 00:10:38,120
Sure. Thank you.

182
00:10:46,440 --> 00:10:47,320
We're all set.

183
00:10:48,279 --> 00:10:49,159
Then let's...

184
00:10:49,559 --> 00:10:50,399
get ready to start.

185
00:10:50,559 --> 00:10:51,240
Okay, okay.

186
00:10:54,440 --> 00:10:55,600
First of all,

187
00:10:56,279 --> 00:10:58,960
December 31st, 1999.

188
00:10:59,000 --> 00:11:00,039
What were you doing that day?

189
00:11:03,000 --> 00:11:04,440
1999?

190
00:11:05,679 --> 00:11:07,120
Oh, good lord.

191
00:11:07,720 --> 00:11:09,159
How many years has it been?

192
00:11:09,720 --> 00:11:10,879
Who could possibly remember that?

193
00:11:12,039 --> 00:11:13,120
A bit tough on you, huh?

194
00:11:13,600 --> 00:11:14,679
Take your time to think.

195
00:11:14,720 --> 00:11:15,360
No rush.

196
00:11:15,519 --> 00:11:16,399
We've got plenty of time.

197
00:11:25,320 --> 00:11:26,320
I think...

198
00:11:27,679 --> 00:11:28,879
I remember a little.

199
00:11:30,960 --> 00:11:32,120
That day...

200
00:11:32,799 --> 00:11:34,240
I think I was with Ma Guowen,

201
00:11:34,240 --> 00:11:36,559
having a meal at a restaurant.

202
00:11:37,080 --> 00:11:37,559
Right.

203
00:11:38,840 --> 00:11:40,320
That was quite a memorable day.

204
00:11:40,919 --> 00:11:41,879
Millennium Eve.

205
00:11:42,120 --> 00:11:45,240
Plus, Lapi Brewery's auction succeeded,

206
00:11:45,840 --> 00:11:46,799
so they held a victory banquet.

207
00:11:47,120 --> 00:11:47,840
You attended too,

208
00:11:47,919 --> 00:11:48,320
didn't you?

209
00:11:49,919 --> 00:11:50,559
Right, right.

210
00:11:52,679 --> 00:11:53,240
Who was there?

211
00:11:55,000 --> 00:11:56,360
At my age...

212
00:11:57,879 --> 00:11:59,240
With a whole table of people,

213
00:11:59,399 --> 00:12:00,519
I can't recall.

214
00:12:02,679 --> 00:12:04,279
Ma Guowen must've been there, right?

215
00:12:04,639 --> 00:12:05,000
Yes.

216
00:12:05,000 --> 00:12:05,519
Right?

217
00:12:06,320 --> 00:12:07,360
Was the deputy director there?

218
00:12:07,360 --> 00:12:07,919
Yes.

219
00:12:08,879 --> 00:12:09,759
So both directors were there.

220
00:12:09,759 --> 00:12:10,799
Was the chief engineer there?

221
00:12:12,600 --> 00:12:13,600
Was Chen Qingchun there?

222
00:12:17,799 --> 00:12:18,360
I think...

223
00:12:18,639 --> 00:12:20,000
I think Old Chen was there.

224
00:12:20,600 --> 00:12:21,159
He was.

225
00:12:21,639 --> 00:12:22,879
"Old Chen"?

226
00:12:23,000 --> 00:12:23,840
Sounds pretty close.

227
00:12:24,879 --> 00:12:25,720
Chen.

228
00:12:25,879 --> 00:12:26,879
Qing.

229
00:12:27,240 --> 00:12:27,720
Chun.

230
00:12:28,960 --> 00:12:29,879
Where did you go afterward?

231
00:12:32,200 --> 00:12:33,000
After it wrapped up,

232
00:12:33,080 --> 00:12:34,240
I went home.

233
00:12:34,600 --> 00:12:35,399
No after-party?

234
00:12:35,720 --> 00:12:36,559
No.

235
00:12:37,159 --> 00:12:38,399
My health wasn't that great.

236
00:12:39,120 --> 00:12:40,919
During dinner, they talked about

237
00:12:41,159 --> 00:12:42,720
going to some karaoke joint.

238
00:12:43,519 --> 00:12:44,639
That Ma Guowen,

239
00:12:44,919 --> 00:12:46,320
he always liked to sing.

240
00:12:46,879 --> 00:12:48,519
Big and burly as he was,

241
00:12:48,759 --> 00:12:50,919
at Lapi Brewery's annual gala,

242
00:12:51,240 --> 00:12:52,240
he actually sang really well.

243
00:12:52,519 --> 00:12:54,080
His specialty was that...

244
00:12:54,240 --> 00:12:54,919
What was it called?

245
00:12:54,919 --> 00:12:55,679
One more from the brewery, Director Zheng.

246
00:12:55,960 --> 00:12:57,039
Do you recognize this car?

247
00:13:08,919 --> 00:13:10,240
20793.

248
00:13:11,679 --> 00:13:12,360
Sound familiar?

249
00:13:18,559 --> 00:13:20,960
Shaking your head means you don't recall?

250
00:13:25,919 --> 00:13:26,519
Director Zheng,

251
00:13:26,840 --> 00:13:27,559
you know as well as anyone

252
00:13:28,440 --> 00:13:29,360
that we didn't bring you in

253
00:13:30,200 --> 00:13:31,519
without good reason.

254
00:13:34,879 --> 00:13:35,960
It has to do with this car.

255
00:13:39,519 --> 00:13:40,799
You're a retired official,

256
00:13:41,879 --> 00:13:42,799
a sensible man.

257
00:13:43,320 --> 00:13:44,559
Don't make us spell it out.

258
00:13:45,120 --> 00:13:46,120
Tell us yourself.

259
00:13:51,279 --> 00:13:52,000
I'll talk.

260
00:13:53,879 --> 00:13:55,039
Chen Qingchun...

261
00:13:55,879 --> 00:13:57,840
begged me to scrap a car for him.

262
00:13:59,120 --> 00:14:00,080
I figured,

263
00:14:00,080 --> 00:14:01,440
since an in-law asked,

264
00:14:02,039 --> 00:14:03,679
I'd take care of it for him.

265
00:14:05,039 --> 00:14:05,879
I admit,

266
00:14:06,039 --> 00:14:07,360
abusing my official position,

267
00:14:07,600 --> 00:14:09,000
I pulled some strings for him.

268
00:14:09,960 --> 00:14:10,519
I deeply regret it.

269
00:14:10,519 --> 00:14:11,639
Were you two in-laws back then?

270
00:14:14,639 --> 00:14:16,679
When did Zheng Xiaoqin and Chen Yuan marry?

271
00:14:17,399 --> 00:14:18,519
What year was that?

272
00:14:24,720 --> 00:14:26,279
Off track, completely off track.

273
00:14:28,039 --> 00:14:28,799
Here's the thing.

274
00:14:29,960 --> 00:14:33,159
You helped Chen Qingchun scrap a car,

275
00:14:33,519 --> 00:14:35,279
and then he got the exact same model.

276
00:14:35,519 --> 00:14:36,440
That's very strange.

277
00:14:36,879 --> 00:14:38,519
I can't figure out why.

278
00:14:40,519 --> 00:14:41,240
As for Old Chen...

279
00:14:41,240 --> 00:14:44,200
why did he buy the exact same car?

280
00:14:45,279 --> 00:14:46,200
I don't know.

281
00:14:50,000 --> 00:14:51,200
I made mistakes.

282
00:14:53,279 --> 00:14:54,360
When Lapi Brewery

283
00:14:55,080 --> 00:14:56,039
was being sold off,

284
00:14:56,360 --> 00:14:57,519
on Ma Guowen's behalf,

285
00:14:57,799 --> 00:14:58,960
I drove down the plant's price,

286
00:14:59,519 --> 00:15:00,399
and helped him

287
00:15:00,399 --> 00:15:01,559
grease some wheels.

288
00:15:02,559 --> 00:15:04,360
I admit I took some...

289
00:15:05,200 --> 00:15:06,200
some kickbacks.

290
00:15:06,799 --> 00:15:09,600
I did commit misconduct in office.

291
00:15:10,000 --> 00:15:10,759
I deeply regret it.

